                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "810e0c93-7d6f-3a9a-b965-11872f5cf2ed",
                        "entry_id": "2f6d47d1-67ba-305e-9e37-97d07f957afb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of various pustular skin conditions."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "24d6f47d-f912-43b2-8597-5c316911c469",
                                "sense_id": "810e0c93-7d6f-3a9a-b965-11872f5cf2ed",
                                "text": "heal this tetter of pedagogism that bespreads him"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d301d186-f7f7-4004-96bc-6b7ea96691d1",
                                "sense_id": "810e0c93-7d6f-3a9a-b965-11872f5cf2ed",
                                "text": "Angelus Politianus had a tetter in his nose continually running, fulsome in company, yet no man so eloquent and pleasing in his works."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9bf7eaf3-167a-440d-8bcc-f4980c5a12e7",
                                "sense_id": "810e0c93-7d6f-3a9a-b965-11872f5cf2ed",
                                "text": "A scabby tetter on their pelts will stick"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a8a2f16-df25-4aa5-86b6-f3988d407225",
                                "sense_id": "810e0c93-7d6f-3a9a-b965-11872f5cf2ed",
                                "text": "She works at St. Veronica’s hospital, lives nearby at the home of a Mrs. Quoad, a lady widowed long ago and since suffering a series of antiquated diseases—greensickness, tetter, kibes, purples, imposthumes and almonds in the ears, most recently a touch of scurvy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7e72be3-0a31-45b9-8065-77c626d28685",
                        "source_entry_id": "2f6d47d1-67ba-305e-9e37-97d07f957afb",
                        "source_sense_id": "810e0c93-7d6f-3a9a-b965-11872f5cf2ed",
                        "source_sense_description": "skin condition",
                        "target_lang_word": "dartre",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "dartre",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f6455365-5c17-3fcc-b714-79d898771bfc",
                                        "entry_id": "a460baa4-7fff-3a30-aade-f1a63ed4e195",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Éruption croûteuse ou exfoliation de l’épiderme qui caractérise certaines maladies de la peau."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b94a34ae-c7da-41e7-bffa-e0eb5942a58f",
                                                "sense_id": "f6455365-5c17-3fcc-b714-79d898771bfc",
                                                "text": "Quant à ma rage de travail, je la comparerai à une dartre. Je me gratte en criant. C’est à la fois un plaisir et un supplice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c4003fd-f8fc-4a53-a72e-1b6d11954b99",
                                                "sense_id": "f6455365-5c17-3fcc-b714-79d898771bfc",
                                                "text": "Ce sont les pharmaciens qui écrivent des lettres, et encore après avoir au préalable mouillé leur langue avec du vinaigre, car autrement leur visage se couvrirait de dartres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6bb3b8e-cbf3-4875-a392-40d76b85ed4b",
                                                "sense_id": "f6455365-5c17-3fcc-b714-79d898771bfc",
                                                "text": "La force dont il maniait l’épée ou l’arquebuse était d’autant plus remarquable qu’il était comme tous les autres, amaigri, mordu de dartres et d’ulcères."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05822723-4dc0-4345-9790-3cae61d9e1d7",
                                                "sense_id": "f6455365-5c17-3fcc-b714-79d898771bfc",
                                                "text": "Dartre farineuse, vive, écailleuse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
